SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
From: fedora-atomic-phone <noreply@fedora-atomic-phone.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: sc8280xp: 32-bit SECONDARY_MI2S_RX on the OnePlus 12

The machine driver's BE fixup runs every back end at 48 kHz, 2 x 16 bit.
On the OnePlus 12 (oneplus,waffle) SECONDARY_MI2S_RX feeds two TFA9874
amplifiers that Android configures for 2 x 32-bit I2S slots (64 bit
clocks per frame, tfa98xx.cnt: TDMNBCK 2, TDMSLLN 31, TDMSSIZE 31). With
2 x 16 bit (32 fs) the amplifier reached its operating state but flagged
a TDM error and a TDM LUT error and stayed silent.

Force S32_LE on that BE on this board only. A module parameter
(waffle_sec_mi2s_bits, 0644, read at every stream start) switches back to
16 bit for comparison without a rebuild.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [board hack; upstream would take the BE
  format from DT or the topology]
Tested: not yet (v9 RAM test)

---
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/sc8280xp.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/sc8280xp.c
@@ -3,6 +3,7 @@
 
 #include <dt-bindings/sound/qcom,q6afe.h>
 #include <linux/module.h>
+#include <linux/of.h>
 #include <linux/platform_device.h>
 #include <sound/soc.h>
 #include <sound/soc-dapm.h>
@@ -288,6 +289,17 @@
 	}
 }
 
+/*
+ * OnePlus 12 (waffle): the TFA9874 speaker amplifiers on SECONDARY_MI2S
+ * are configured by Android for 2 x 32-bit I2S slots (64 bit clocks per
+ * frame); with the generic 2 x 16 bit (32 fs) they report a TDM error and
+ * stay silent. 32 by default, 16 to compare; read at every stream start.
+ */
+static unsigned int waffle_sec_mi2s_bits = 32;
+module_param(waffle_sec_mi2s_bits, uint, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(waffle_sec_mi2s_bits,
+		 "OnePlus 12: SECONDARY_MI2S_RX sample width, 32 (default) or 16");
+
 static int sc8280xp_be_hw_params_fixup(struct snd_soc_pcm_runtime *rtd,
 				     struct snd_pcm_hw_params *params)
 {
@@ -309,6 +321,13 @@
 	case TX_CODEC_DMA_TX_3:
 		channels->min = 1;
 		break;
+	case SECONDARY_MI2S_RX:
+		if (of_machine_is_compatible("oneplus,waffle") &&
+		    waffle_sec_mi2s_bits == 32) {
+			snd_mask_none(fmt);
+			snd_mask_set_format(fmt, SNDRV_PCM_FORMAT_S32_LE);
+		}
+		break;
 	default:
 		break;
 	}
